{"id":"83232df3aa7b3b3902e2275dcd4e35b111122a6e","axis":"silent","repo":"strapi/strapi","sha":"83232df3aa7b3b3902e2275dcd4e35b111122a6e","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/docs/packages/core/content-manager/index.md","lines":["@@ -44,18 +44,23 @@ The edit view response holds only a count for each relation field, and the relat"," "," `server/src/history` and `admin/src/history` hold the content history feature. It is an Enterprise feature, gated by `cms-content-history`. When the gate is off, the plugin still registers the `historyVersion` model so that no data is lost."," ","-History records the writes made through the Content Manager routes. Each version stores the source of the write, and the versions list shows it as a tag:","+History records the writes made through the Content Manager routes and through the Content API (REST and GraphQL). Each version stores the source of the write, and the versions list shows it as a tag:"," ","-| Source        | Write made with                              |","-| ------------- | -------------------------------------------- |","-| `admin-panel` | An admin panel session                       |","-| `admin-api`   | An admin token on the Content Manager routes |","+| Source        | Write made with                                                                                                                           |","+| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |","+| `admin-panel` | Any admin strategy that sets a user on the Content Manager routes, except an admin token. This includes SSO and the strategies of plugins |","+| `admin-api`   | An admin token on the Content Manager routes                                                                                              |","+| `content-api` | Any request on a Content API route                                                                                                        |"," ","-Each version also stores a reference to its author: a type, and the model and document id of the author record. An admin panel write is attributed to the admin. An admin token write is attributed to the token, not to its owner. The versions list shows the current name of the author. A version of a deleted admin shows \"Deleted user\", and a version of a deleted token shows \"Deleted token\". The reference stays on the version after a delete. A document id is never given to another record, so the reference never points to a newer author.","+History records nothing for the other writes: a write on another admin route, a write made outside a request, and a Content API write when `admin.history.contentApi.enabled` is `false`."," ","-The `createdBy` relation is saved and returned from the history route as backward support for third-party usage. But it is now deprecated, and the `author` fields should be used instead.","+Each version also stores a reference to its author: a type, and the model and document id of the author record. A write made with an admin panel session is attributed to the admin. An admin token write is attributed to the token, not to its owner. A Content API write made with an API token is attributed to that token. A Content API write made by a logged-in end user is attributed to that end user. The author of an `admin-panel` write is always the admin of the request, whatever the admin strategy. For the other sources, the author comes from the authentication strategy of the request: each strategy that can give an author is registered with the history feature, and the Users & Permissions plugin registers its own. These writes have no author when the request has no authentication, when it is a public write, or when it uses a strategy that is not registered. The versions list shows no author for these versions. For the other versions, the versions list shows the current name of the author. A version of a deleted admin or end user shows \"Deleted user\", and a version of a deleted token shows \"Deleted token\". The reference stays on the version after a delete. A document id is never given to another record, so the reference never points to a newer author."," ","-Versions saved before the source and the author existed show as `admin-panel`. Their author is the admin of `createdBy`.","+Set `admin.history.contentApi.enabled` to `false` to stop recording Content API writes. It is `true` by default. The flag does not change Content Manager writes.","+","+The `createdBy` relation is saved and returned from the history route as backward support for third-party usage. But it is now deprecated, and the `author` fields should be used instead. It is empty for Content API writes.","+","+Versions saved before the source and the author existed show as `admin-panel`. Their author is the admin of `createdBy`. An admin token write of that time also shows as `admin-panel`, and its author is the owner of the token."," "," The `preview` folders hold the live preview. Read [Live preview](./06-preview.md). The `history` and `preview` folders carry their own `LICENSE` file."," "],"additions":13,"deletions":8,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/docs/packages/plugins/users-permissions/index.md","lines":["@@ -22,12 +22,13 @@ The plugin adds three content types. `plugin::users-permissions.user` (table `up"," "," ### `register`"," ","-[`server/src/register.js`](https://github.com/strapi/strapi/blob/develop/packages/plugins/users-permissions/server/src/register.js) does four things:","+[`server/src/register.js`](https://github.com/strapi/strapi/blob/develop/packages/plugins/users-permissions/server/src/register.js) does five things:"," "," - It registers the strategy `users-permissions` for the `content-api` auth scope, with `strapi.get('auth').register`."," - It adds a `content-api.output` sanitizer that removes the `users` relation from role entities."," - It calls `server/src/graphql` when the `graphql` plugin exists. That code disables queries and mutations on permissions, replaces the create, update and delete mutations of users and roles, and adds the `me` query and the auth mutations (`login`, `register` and the password and email flows)."," - It registers a hand-written OpenAPI spec (`documentation/content-api.yaml`) with the `documentation` plugin when it exists.","+- It tells the Content Manager how to find the end user who made a Content API write, when Content History is enabled. A Content API write by an end user then shows the end user as its author. Read [History and preview](../../core/content-manager/index.md#history-and-preview) for the rule."," "," ### Authentication strategy"," "],"additions":2,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/core/content-manager/admin/src/history/components/VersionsList.tsx","lines":["@@ -213,6 +213,10 @@ const SOURCE_LABELS: Record<HistoryVersions.HistoryVersionSource, MessageDescrip","     id: 'content-manager.history.sidebar.version-card.source.admin-api',","     defaultMessage: 'Admin API',","   },","+  'content-api': {","+    id: 'content-manager.history.sidebar.version-card.source.content-api',","+    defaultMessage: 'Content API',","+  },"," };"," "," const VersionSource = ({ source }: { source: HistoryVersions.HistoryVersionSource }) => {"],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/core/content-manager/admin/src/translations/en.json","lines":["@@ -371,6 +371,7 @@","   \"history.sidebar.version-card.deleted-author.token\": \"Deleted token\",","   \"history.sidebar.version-card.source.admin-panel\": \"Admin panel\",","   \"history.sidebar.version-card.source.admin-api\": \"Admin API\",","+  \"history.sidebar.version-card.source.content-api\": \"Content API\",","   \"history.sidebar.versionDescription\": \"{distanceToNow}{isAnonymous, select, true {} other { by {author}}}{isCurrent, select, true { <b>(current)</b>} other {}}\",","   \"history.sidebar.show-newer\": \"Show newer versions\",","   \"his